{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327813-rumors-changelings-the-gentry-and-the-hedge-between-them","id":327813,"title":"Rumors: Changelings, the Gentry, and the Hedge between them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T22:47:13-08:00","id":327813,"title":"Rumors: Changelings, the Gentry, and the Hedge between them","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/download/2ls4xd2jn5bf5pj/World+of+Darkness+Rumors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/download/2ls4xd2jn5bf5pj/World+of+Darkness+Rumors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/download/2ls4xd2jn5bf5pj/World+of+Darkness+Rumors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mediafire.com/download/2ls4xd2jn5bf5pj/World+of+Darkness+Rumors.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Based on this file, I'm spearheading a 2.0 Rumors project to create even more awesome plot hooks, story ideas, and paradigm shifts that anyone can use at their table. If you have an awesome idea for a rumor, story, or legend, post it here, and by next February we'll decide who's story passed the bar to be included.<br /> <br /> This thread is focused on changelings, the true fae, and the world that brings them apart; ideas not pertaining to these in some form will automatically not be included.<br /> <br /> Ready...set...go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:48:56-08:00","id":328518,"title":"","content":"&quot;Everything has a parallel. We have our Fetches. The Gentry have their nemesis. This is how the Wyrd like it- a symmetric enemy can always create the best story. However, the Wyrd itself have its own &quot;enemy&quot;- the Echo. Think about it as a second fate which manipulates the world to contradict the Wyrd's efforts. If you can learn how to manipulate that fate, no Gentry will be able to touch you ever again. There is, of course, a price. There is always a price&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T18:03:59-08:00","id":328810,"title":"","content":"&quot;Wanna hear something interesting? You see, a long time ago I was minding my own business tasting the latest beverage made out of goblin fruit in our beloved tavern when something caught my attention. There was this weird looking guy that...oh come on don't look at me like that, he was weirder than..look he was an outsider OK? it wasn't the regular weird we have here now let me tell my story. Now where was I? Oh yes, I was bored and a little bit tipsy so I decided to go and talk to this stranger, see if he had any interesting stories to tell. He was suspicious at first but I used my natural charm to get him to talk...and a couple of pints, you know, just to get in a friendly atmosphere. Well, turns out that the guy was a wandering sorcerer looking for components for an experiment. Apparently he had made a major breakthrough regarding some occult principle of the mind or something like that. Wait a sec..glup glup...&quot;<br /> &quot;Ah that's the stuff...telling stories always makes me thirsty. Anyway he explained it to me and if I understood him correctly, it's all about limits you know? You see, this world is solid an exists regardless what we think or feel, it limits our minds. Its like our minds are water and reality the jar, it prevents us from going crazy, keeps us sane by forcing our minds to take form. However in the hedge and arcadia? not so much, reality is shaped by your feelings and thoughts so your mind spills all over the place, incapable of fixing itself and constantly changing shape. So the key to keep yourself sane in there? I'll let you think about it while I drink.&quot;<br /> &quot;Damn it! empty. Hey! another pint here please! storyteller doing his job!...ok lets continue. The answer is simple: anchor your mind in the real world. He told me that it was possible to make an special kind of contract with an aspect of reality and fix a part of yourself in this world...or was it a human anchored in reality? can't remember right, too much drink, it happens. Well, he told me that It helps in several ways: first it gives you the certainty that there is a real world making you, if not inmune, very resistant to the loss of clarity, second it acts as a beacon, like a lighthouse to guide you back and third and most impressive of all you could boost the signal of your connection so you can bring a piece of reality with you to arcadia! how about that? amazing isn't it?. What did you say? If it's true? Ha! it's way to good to be true if you ask me and honestly it felt like the guy was boasting more than anything else. Ah but if it were true? then we would have one hell of an advantage in our war against the gentry.&quot;<br /> &quot;Glup glup...puagh! this one is not so good, oh well a drink is a drink. What's that? where is he right now? no idea, we both passed out drinking and when I woke up he was gone. However I remember him mentioning something about going to L.A. hum....oh, I can see it in your face, you wanna go after him? fine, waste your time if that is what you want but if and only if you find him and turns out to be true have the courtesy to pay me a visit. I'm sure you will have one hell of a story to tell.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-03-2014, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T23:29:59-08:00","id":329913,"title":"","content":"&quot;There's a rumor about a new entitlement going around, calling themselves the Trusted Confederacy of the Underdog. Apparently they're the tricksters against authority, helping out the little guy and all. Yeah, it's great at first, but then they wind up turning around on the people they help once the problem's solved. And who always wants to cause trouble and play everyone and every angle? Because it sure isn't Rumpelstiltskin out there sparking riots.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T11:00:27-08:00","id":333222,"title":"","content":"&quot;Have you ever wondered why the Gentry always put fetches in our place when they take us? Sure, it covers up our disappearance, but why would they care about that? They don't live here, and they don't care about getting caught. So why go through the trouble of making perfect duplicates?<br /> <br /> Maybe the Fetch isn't the duplicate.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:53:46-08:00","id":333351,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#373E4D\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Everyone dies once their time is up, despite how. Except there's someone or something killing people and inside them, there's sand.<br /> Autumn Court thinks it's something to do with dying before your time.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1740-soirgriffe","name":"Soirgriffe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T16:56:25-08:00","id":336482,"title":"","content":"&quot;Maybe the Fetch isn't... What? Are you high?<br /> <br /> Look, dude, quit your existential whining and go kill your fetch. You'll see, it's just a pile of twigs and pocket lint. No more worrying about whether you're the real deal.<br /> <br /> You're right to wonder about why they make the fetches, though. People go missing all the time, there's no reason to cover up one or two more. Unless it's not just one or two. I mean, there's what, a couple hundred changelings, just in this little city? And we're just the lucky ones, the ones who escaped. How many more of us are there still trapped in Faerie? The Keepers go through so much trouble to take so many people, and I don't think it's just so they have puppies to kick. No, they're planning something big.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}